_audit_update_record             
;
2020-11-18 deposited with the CCDC.	2026-11-05 downloaded from the CCDC.
;
_vrf_PLAT035_BS_AC139            
;
PROBLEM: _chemical_absolute_configuration Info  Not Given     Please Do!     
RESPONSE: This is a monoclinic Molybdenum dataset collected with BRUKER 
APEX II CCD diffractometer. Absolute configuration established by the 
structure determination (using rm or ad etc commands) of a compound
containing a chiral reference molecule of known absolute configuration
or established by anomalous dispersion effects in diffraction measurements
on the crystal is not possible in Mo K alfa X ray source. Therefore
absolute configuration is unknown from structure solution and an arbitrary
choice of enantiomer cannot be made. It could be possible with some regions
of reciprocal space those remain unaccessible to three circle goniometers,
especially at the high 2 Theta angles that are needed to collect
high resolution copper data. 
;

_vrf_PLAT417_BS_AC139            
;
PROBLEM Short Inter D-H..H-D       H3B..H14B .   1.88 Ang.  
                           x,y,z  =      1_555 Check
RESPONSE: Short non-bonding inter D-H..H-D contacts are related to
disordered or misplaced H-atoms. Hydrogens atoms H3B and H14B are
located from electron density maps, however DFIX command has been
used to fix its coordinates. Thus such intermolecular H...H
separation at 1.88 Angstroms between unit-occupancy H atoms
may be wrongly oriented.
;
_vrf_PLAT420_BS_AC139            
;
PROBLEM: D-H Without Acceptor O14 --H14B  .   Please Check      
RESPONSE: H14B is located from electron density map and
DFIX command is used to fix its coordinate. It is not appropriate
to locate the exact position of hydrogens in presence of heavy
metal atom. So H14B atom is likely to be be wrongly
oriented and missing an appropriate acceptor atom. 
;



